# "Whenever you attack": Raffine stays home on turn 3 while the Thraben Inspector attacks alone, and the Inspector connives 1
# (X is the one attacking creature): it draws an Island and discards it. On turn 4 Bot2's Ornithopter attacks and Bot1 is asked
# nothing (the refused Choose: a connive would ask what to discard): the trigger is for its controller's attacks only.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Raffine, Scheming Seer
Plains
Thraben Inspector
Island
Island
Lightning Bolt
Island
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Raffine, Scheming Seer.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Thraben Inspector.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Thraben Inspector > Bot2)
Bot1.Choose(Island)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Graveyard = Island
[T4 Bot2.DeclareAttackers]
Bot2.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot1)
! Bot1.Choose
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Island
Bot1.Battlefield.Thraben Inspector.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
